<title>USA: MCA motion picture VP Busby resigns.</title>
<headline>MCA motion picture VP Busby resigns.</headline>
<dateline>UNIVERSAL CITY, Calif. 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>MCA Inc Thursday said Ann Busby has resigned her position as senior vice president, MCA Motion Picture Group.</p>
<p>In a statement, Busby said she is leaving to pursue a &quot;number of new opportunities which have been presented to me.&quot;</p>
<p>MCA said it has no plans to replace Busby.</p>
<p>Separately, MCA's Home Entertainment Group named Alexander Trauttmansdorff-Weinsberg to the newly-created position of vice president for Pay television and Television Business development for Universal Pay Television. He will be based in Munich. MCA is a unit of Seagram Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
